{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin","id":1468360,"title":"Spirits, Gift teaching, and Ronin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-19T11:35:27-08:00","id":1468360,"title":"Spirits, Gift teaching, and Ronin","content":"For a while now I've been thinking about ways to expand the use of Ronin in my chronicles as an ST. I think they are often an underutilized part of the setting. One issue that I've had is that Ronin don't have Rank and thus can't learn Gifts from spirits since Gifts are linked to Rank. Instead, they learn them from other Garou which essentially means other Ronin, and that limits what Gifts are available. Another option is to learn from Banes, but that is limiting from a character and ST perspective because it becomes a corruption story at that point.<br /> <br /> However, I now think I may have been too restrictive on that. After rereading what's written on both Ronin and Skin Dancers, it seems clear that they can learn Gifts from spirits provided those are \u201cunassociated spirits\u201d as the W20 corebook describes them. And that these two Garou, despite not having Ranks, can learn Gifts of any level... provided they can find spirits willing to teach them.<br /> <br /> So that got me thinking, what kind of spirits are willing to teach Ronin Gifts?<br /> <br /> Obviously none of the spirits that belong to one of the spirit broods of the Garou tribal totems shouldn't do so. (There could always be atypical individual spirits that would normally be part of a brood, but for whatever reason doesn't belong to one despite similar spirits belonging. But they wouldn't be normal.)<br /> <br /> I then wondered whether any of the broods belonging to any of the other Fera might be willing to do so, especially those breeds most antagonistic to the Garou. But I decided against it. Ultimately those spirits follow the same laws as everyone else, and they shouldn't be willing to teach Gifts to an outcast, rankless Changing Breed as it would shortchange their own Fera who need still need to follow their own Rank = Level system.<br /> <br /> So these \u201cunassociated spirits\u201d should either be spirits that don't belong to any brood, or belong to some theoretical brood that is clearly separate from those broods associated with the Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> We know Minotaur is one such spirit, and he might have a small brood of his own (the Minotaur pack totem description says \u201cplaces his children in contact wit spirits that can teach them Gifts, and thus his children can learn most Gifts of Rank Three or lower.\u201d). What other kind of spirits should Minotaur have access to that he could put Skin Dancers into contact with them?<br /> <br /> Tick, from the Skinner SAS, could be another. That spirit is clearly looking for power and willing to not follow the normal rules. Since he's shown as a Skin Dancer totem, it's likely he was already one of those spirits Minotaur used to teach Gifts to children.<br /> <br /> What other \u201cabandoned\u201d or \u201cignored\u201d spirits would be willing to defy the Pact? Minotaur is not a direct servant of the Wyrm but does bear a faint touch of taint from the Beast-of-War. Tick is mentioned as a Totem of Cunning. While I don't think this means that the canonical Gaian totems of Cunning mentioned in the sourcebooks fit here, I do think we need to thinking about spirits that would seem to fit into the Cunning category. And we could also look at spirits that might be partially corrupted, but not yet fallen.<br /> <br /> So Bat might make a good example if we follow the idea that Bat is schizophrenic with one aspect fallen and one aspect redeemed. Since Ronin are inbetween these two extremes, surely some Bat spirits should be open to this.<br /> <br /> The W20 White Howlers tribebook gives us Carrion Bird totem. This totem primarily serves BSD packs, but it also implies that Gaian Garou can do so well as well provided they are willing to lose Honor Renown and be viewed as possibly Wyrm tainted by the other Garou. So once again we have a totem that straddles the line between corrupt and Gaian.<br /> <br /> In terms of non-canonical spirits, should we follow Tick's example and look at other parasitical animals like lice, leeches, lampreys? Disreputable animals that spread disease like houseflies? (We know not all such animals would fit here \u2013 the game has Gaian totems like Cuckoo, Flea and Tsetse Fly, and the Wendigo brood includes tundra mosquitoes.)<br /> <br /> Are there examples of spirits the Garou have ignored, spurned, or offended who also might fit into this category? <br /> <br /> I'm especially looking for ideas of non-corrupted Gaian spirits that may nevertheless operate outside the restrictions established by the Pact. They might be dark or treacherous spirits, but not tainted. The scorpion, for example, is an animal often associated with treachery because it is in its nature per the fable the Scorpion and the Frog. It might be a spirit that is open to teaching Gifts to such outcast Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T13:57:34-08:00","id":1468425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin#post1468360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue that I've had is that Ronin don't have Rank and thus can't learn Gifts from spirits since Gifts are linked to Rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that one book clearly states, that this is not true. That, in fact any spirit could bestow any Gift in its portfolio on any Fera, if thy are physically capable of using the gift and that linking Gifts to certain Ranks is simply a measure of balancing the game.I thought it was ST Handbook revised, but I can't find the passage there, so it might have been another book.<br /> <br /> Totems can allow packmembers of packs in their service to use Gifts regardless of rank and some Gifts are in different ranks in different lists.<br /> <br /> In our LARP we have vague guidelines on how much XP a character of a certain rank should have in total. So, if a Ronin-NPC would surpass this limits we'd assume that the character has gained some standing. It would still be nigh impossible to get Gifts usually limited to a tribe, and hard to get Gifts tied exclusively to an auspice, even the character's own, if the character didn't at least value his auspices in a small but meaningful way. But Breed Gifts as well as Gifts that appear on multiple lists are things the character might get, if the Ronin is able to find the right spirit and convince it. The rule of thumb, that a caern of a caern rating equal to the rank of the Gift needs to be visited to find a spirit is usually overturned when the Ronin does spend an excessive amount of time searching or summons the proper spirit.<br /> <br /> I wonder, where I read that about Gifts. I'll keep looking and will post, if I find the site reference, but if someone else knows, please post it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T16:10:15-08:00","id":1468434,"title":"","content":"I also have the same impression as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a>. Although I don't remember where I saw it, I don't remember either ever reading that spirits cant teach a gift to a Ronin for any reason. I always got the impression that spirits pay far less attention to Garou social rules than the Garou believe.<br /> <br /> What I see is the lists and Rank as guidelines that represent relationships that have already a tradition or history behind it. When judging if you're worth the effort Rank gives an easy start, compatible lists mean the spirit already have a history of dealing with those particular types, and so on.<br /> <br /> But a blank slate relationship isn't a bad one, just one that demands more effort. A Ronin would have to work towards building those bridges from scratch, but that's it, and since it is just for them it is hard, but doable.<br /> <br /> At most I can see some Tribe members being less than pleased about it and actively interfering against it. It is possible that most individual spirits relatively accessible to &quot;list members&quot; are wary of displeasing their usual charges, due to whatever repercussions those can bring. It is also possible that those Garou won't take it lightly to have non-members running around with &quot;their&quot; Gifts. But it only means a Ronin should have a harder time learning and probably has to put some effort in not rubbing it against everyone's faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T19:52:19-08:00","id":1468451,"title":"","content":"Regardless how strict and universal certain rules are, Rank and level of Gift are clearly linked together. And the Pact has to mean something. Those were the terms originally agreed upon, and spirits can certainly violate the Pact, but they also pay a price for violating chiminage just like Garou do. And in terms of Ronin, it's also pretty clear they have a more obstacles learning from spirits than Garou who are not Ronin. So clearly this is a big issue.<br /> <br /> The next paragraph down I said that I was too restrictive in my previous thoughts on it. Other places do say that there are spritis even Ronin can work with. So the entire point of the post is to think of the kind of spirits most willing to work with these Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T02:05:24-08:00","id":1468471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468451#post1468451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Pact has to mean something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but what? For the longest time the Pact was unclear, not sure if the terms were printed in recent years.<br /> <br /> So, basically the Pact was in broadest terms that garou defend Gaia (or fera do the jobs they were created for, kitsune do whatever they want) and the spritis will asist them in their endevours by bestowing Gifts upon them, answer to Rites and as extension to that submit to the Rite of Binding and Rite of Fetish. Obvoiously there was enough leaway for the spirits and certain groups of fera (changing breeds, tribes, etc.) to form seconday commitments in the spirit of the Pact, like exclusitity of certain powers to certain groups.<br /> <br /> And, while the spirit community and the garou community might have relative strict ideas on what &quot;doing the job they were created for&quot; might mean, any individual spirit/Ronin interaction might adhere to those ideas or not. I mean, most Silver Fangs and Shadowlord (as presented in 1st edition) might think the Bone Gnawers do nothing, and therefore would violate the Pact. The whole 1st Editon TB Bone Gnawer, iirc, was a report of a Shadow Lord to some Silver Fangs on the question, if the Bone Gnawers should be wiped out... wasn't it?<br /> <br /> <br /> What spirits might be most willing to work with Ronin? Well, I gues those who have been overlooked a lot before... which might be different regionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T02:22:47-08:00","id":1468473,"title":"","content":"Rank and level of Gift are connected, but the book also says explicitly that this can be waived if the spirit so decides. I see it as first indicator that any spirit may be persuaded into breaking the rules under the right circumstances. Not that Ronins don't gave a tougher time, but that exceptions may occur in many ways.<br /> <br /> I don't remember reading much on the Pact, so I would like some points to where go for it to have a better grasp of this part. I personally never liked the notion of the spirit world bowing so much to the rules of the Tribes, but that's another thing.<br /> <br /> Also, there are other situations that outright indicate that spirits not always do things by the rules, sometimes in far more glaring ways than teaching Ronin, like how Cockroach is kind of adopting the Samsa Breed and teaching them Gifts.<br /> <br /> On which spirits would be more likely to do that, I think it would be the more overlooked ones. Spirits that have no contact with the peoples the Garou live among, spirits of things too inconspicuous or easily mistaken as other, more well known spirits.<br /> <br /> The dubious nature of spirits like Tick and Minotaur makes sense for relatively high-profile spirits dealing with Ronin, as those are the spirits more likely to be pressed by circumstances to position themselves and sought by Garou when their position is known. Spirits of little-known species, almost unheard-off technologies and so on, especially if they're too easily mistaken with other well known spirits, are the most likely to be out of any broader accord or so rarely sought to not make a difference.<br /> <br /> You can also decide to focus on spirits from the High Umbra. AFAIK the Garou have little understanding of the place and its spirits, but it isn't impossible for them to travel there, just harder. Those spirits are unlikely to be bound to the same rules and expectations as their Middle Umbra &quot;cousins&quot;, and are a good way to give Ronin potential access to Gifts above level 3.<br /> <br /> But I think the main point should be to let the PCs come up ideas on how to find a spirit that may teach them, and think what are the intrinsic difficulties that would justify most Ronin not going that route. Individual spirits that teach Ronin may exact heft prices or be far more recluse than others of their kind, and must be tracked specifically, as they're individuals. &quot;Forgotten&quot; spirits may be willing to teach only those who can not only find them, but identify them correctly, maybe even having a reputation for refusing Garou because they don't teach Gifts when mistaken. Astral Spirits are naturally hard to reach and harder still for Garou to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T03:12:22-08:00","id":1468478,"title":"","content":"In our LARP game, I tend to create obstacles for a lot of player ideas involving &quot;finding a spirit that should have a certain power advantageous in our situation and make it help us&quot; by making spirits not that cooperative or stating that the players need to find certain items to summon a spirit powerful enough to do, what they want, because, spirits are relatively rare, and those you find are most often gaffelings. And sure, they can do, what you want, but their dice pool is low, so success isn't guaranteed, especially if they are opposing some NPC or environmental force.<br /> <br /> Magic is about balance and plot solving is about putting in an effort. In any case, if a certain power is akin to an obscure Gift, I usually state that the players should petition for that Gift and show they are worthy - and pay the 5XP per level... (in addition to our rules that limits the number of Gifts any character can have, where Gifts not on their respective lists are factored in thrice).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T15:01:21-08:00","id":1468704,"title":"","content":"On the conceptual side of things it\u2019s definitely going to be spirits that exist on a more dangerous, or at least a more individualist and unorthodox sphere then what Garou society is typically comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Garou society despite being as antisocial as it can sometimes be is still heavily social, with packs as the atomic unit of Garou society and both the wolf and human social instincts manifesting with heavy investment in community. While human influences from the homids can lead this to become a society of hierarchies and orthodoxies, the matter remains that Garou society is highly social and this expands to the spirits it has long standing relationships with.<br /> <br /> So them for a Ronin (or Lone Wolf as I usually prefer calling them), they have the difficult task of finding spirits that will be willing to work with them and thus most likely they will not have major pre-existing relations with the Garou Nation or have a natural suspicion or contradiction for working with creatures that have become alienated from society and tradition.<br /> <br /> So as far as animals are concerned then, it seems that any animal with a strong association with family or social values is going to be off the table, alongside traditional tribal totems and Garou spirit patrons. Spirits which have associations with independence or unorthodoxy will probably be more amenable to negotiations, such as many Big Cat spirits or several Reptilian spirits. <br /> <br /> I also imagine that Lone Wolves could have some success with spirits of natural phenomena that are either agnostic or even contradictory to tradition and society. Spirits such as weather phenomena like Thunder Storm or Wildfire might provide patronage for lone wolves, although they\u2019re no doubt going to have strong Wyld-influences. This however seems somewhat unavoidable as I imagine that most Weaver-influenced spirits are going to be disturbed by a Lone Wolves rejection of social order while most wise alone Wolves ought to avoid Wyrm-influenced spirits lest they become recruitment targets of the Black Spiral Dancers (although that\u2019s not to say Maggot or Carrion Bird couldn\u2019t work as hypothetical spirit patrons for a Lone Wolf).<br /> <br /> To briefly cover other concepts that come to mind - I think most material and plant spirits would be difficult to work with as they\u2019re probably already comfortable with ancient relationships established to the Garou Nation although perhaps things like Rivers or mountains prone to Landslides or Seismic Shifts might be more amenable to a change of direction as could plants that are more inconstant and transitory or perhaps even are of an invasive nature. I think most spirits associated with humans will probably be uncomfortable with social outcasts (except of course those human spirits who are themselves associated with outcasts such as Circus, Thief, Pariah, Stray, Revolutionary, Ecstasy, Wrath, etc.). <br /> <br /> Dealing with many of these spirits would likely be dangerous and I agree that it would probably likely include heavier investments for establish relationships rather then calling on pre-existing ones but I also think it could be done and could even be used to demonstrate how there are other ways that things can be done then what is the orthodoxy of the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 11-23-2021, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T15:32:15-08:00","id":1468788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468704#post1468704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the conceptual side of things it\u2019s definitely going to be spirits that exist on a more dangerous, or at least a more individualist and unorthodox sphere then what Garou society is typically comfortable with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in general terms, but an added difficulty for me is that I try hard to put spirits into broods, and that adds an additional complication. Now not all spirits belong to broods, but the vast majority do. And if those broods are associated with the Garou tribes or Changing Breeds, then that brood would be much more likely to follow the Rank=Gift level principal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468704#post1468704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits which have associations with independence or unorthodoxy will probably be more amenable to negotiations, such as many Big Cat spirits or several Reptilian spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave some thought along these lines until I realized that big cat spirits would still belong to a brood associated with the Bastet, and likewise many reptile spirits with the Mokole and Nagah. They aren't Garou tribal totems, but such spirits still follow the same lines in regards to Rank and Gift level for their related Changing Breeds. If they follow the rule with them, then they should follow the rule with Ronin Garou (or the equivalent of Ronin among Bastet and others) and not teach them because they don't have Rank. (While Axis Mundi described explicit broods belonging to each Incarna of the Garou tribes, it didn't give us equivalent broods belonging to the Changing Breeds, so it is easy to forget or ignore that such broods should exist in the setting.)<br /> <br /> Now that doesn't mean some spirits that theoretically do belong to one of those broods might not be an exile or outcast itself and do its own thing. But such things are rare. But this would be a starting point for an ST to create such a spirit and give it a background on why it choose to exist on its own and not be protected by the Incarna leading that brood.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to look at exceptions to the general rule of big cat spirits belong to the brood that normally provide the Bastet their Gifts and patronage. For example, we don't have an changing breed based on ocelots. (Yeah, ocelots are small, but there's other smaller cats among the Bastet.) So maybe Ocelot is a dissatisfied because of that. It is not unfriendly to the Bastet, but also isn't as tightly bound to them. So many ocelot spirits make up their own group distinct from the larger &quot;Bastet brood&quot;, or there's a lot of &quot;bad&quot; ocelot spirits who do their own thing. These could be willing to teach outcats Garou and Fera gifts. But I don't think standard tiger, leopard, lynx, etc. spirits would. The hard part is figuring out individual spirits that may buck trends given that the default is to assume most Gaian spirits belong to one of the aligned broods. But that's why I asked the question.<br /> <br /> Some other thought - maybe ape and monkey spirits? They are often considered to be foolish in folktales, don't have an obvious brood to belong to, and are frequently mentioned in derogatory manner by Garou and Fera (mainly be their use of it as an insult to homids and humans).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468704#post1468704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also imagine that Lone Wolves could have some success with spirits of natural phenomena that are either agnostic or even contradictory to tradition and society. Spirits such as weather phenomena like Thunder Storm or Wildfire might provide patronage for lone wolves, although they\u2019re no doubt going to have strong Wyld-influences. This however seems somewhat unavoidable as I imagine that most Weaver-influenced spirits are going to be disturbed by a Lone Wolves rejection of social order while most wise alone Wolves ought to avoid Wyrm-influenced spirits lest they become recruitment targets of the Black Spiral Dancers (although that\u2019s not to say Maggot or Carrion Bird couldn\u2019t work as hypothetical spirit patrons for a Lone Wolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something like Thunder Storm is probably too tied to Grandfather Thunder to teach Gifts to Ronin. But something like Wildfire could be on its own. Overall, I agree that spirits more aligned to the Wyld would be more willing to teach Gifts (provided the Ronin have a means to communicate with them; I don't think a spirit like Wildfire would know the Garou Tongue, and someone with Spirit Speech would be needed to communicate with it) as by their nature they are uncontrollable, whimsical, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468704#post1468704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dealing with many of these spirits would likely be dangerous and I agree that it would probably likely include heavier investments for establish relationships rather then calling on pre-existing ones but I also think it could be done and could even be used to demonstrate how there are other ways that things can be done then what is the orthodoxy of the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that any spirit that potentially is agreeable to teach a Gift to Ronin would be more dangerous to approach and would demand heavier chiminage than normal. I think that's fine. It creates more story, and gives another reason for Garou to be hostile to Ronin. Ronin who are known to be increasing their Gifts might have made strange chiminages that normal Garou would think is dangerous or harmful to their interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T09:21:38-08:00","id":1468842,"title":"","content":"There is an aspect that should also be considered about ronin and gifts; Why are they ronin in the first place? That would affect a lot of their approaches to spirits and broods in general.<br /> <br /> A garou who was exiled for a crime would know of broods and ways to communicate with the spirits. Thus they would at least know how to approach them correctly and might even still have ties to their breed and auspice broods (after all, a ronin is a tribeless garou, not a garou without breed and auspice.) They might have to do extra work, but they would still be without the brood's respect. After all, ronin technically DO earn renown. Just at a VERY glacial pace.<br /> <br /> However, if the ronin is one who rejected garou nation, they would not have even the breed or auspice ties. Depending on whether the ronin refuses 'magic' in general, they might try to avoid gifts or seek them out the 'human' way (ie. pagan summoning and such.)<br /> <br /> For these ronin, I think their actions would attract spirits. Like if a ronin has managed to terrorize a small town, they might attract banes or spirits of dominance. Refusal to be a werewolf and halting changes and feral behaviour might attract Weaver spirits.<br /> <br /> These are just ideas.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T12:23:28-08:00","id":1468862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468842#post1468842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an aspect that should also be considered about ronin and gifts; Why are they ronin in the first place? That would affect a lot of their approaches to spirits and broods in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that the specific offense of the Ronin that caused his exile is an additional complicating factor, but personally I think that is something that would only add more difficulty to the baseline, not lessen the difficulty from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468842#post1468842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A garou who was exiled for a crime would know of broods and ways to communicate with the spirits. Thus they would at least know how to approach them correctly and might even still have ties to their breed and auspice broods (after all, a ronin is a tribeless garou, not a garou without breed and auspice.) They might have to do extra work, but they would still be without the brood's respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this really depends on the individual Ronin. An Athro Theurge who is now Ronin would have an immense knowledge of the spirit world and many powers that could be used to befriend or coerce spirits. A Cliath Ahroun would likely have only cursory knowledge and lack any details that would be useful IMO. Even a Cliath Theurge would be under severe disadvantage as he has much to learn.<br /> <br /> As for the question of breed and auspice, spirits that teach Gifts of that nature are still bound by the Pact. It's not clear there are &quot;breed broods&quot; or &quot;auspice broods&quot;. Unlike the tribal Incarna broods, we've never been told that these broods exist nor what Incarna would be in charge of them. While Luna, or one of her Incarna avatars, would have a brood of her own consisting of Lunes and and similar moon spirits, it's not clear that all spirtis who teach auspice Gifts are part of that brood. Since the same Gift can appear on multiple tribal lists, can be found in both breed and tribal, auspice and tribal, and auspice and breed; I'm leery of accepting the idea that there are such broods based on breed or auspice. Clearly Luna is involved in some way since she blesses Garou with their auspice, but I don't think that means all spirits who teach Gifts of that auspice are part of her brood. I just think it means she &quot;authorizes&quot; spirits to teach that (and we know that out-of-auspice Gifts can still be purchased just at a higher XP cost and whatever added obstacles an ST wants to provide). And even if for some reason such breeds do exist, they're still impacted by the Rite of the Lone Wolf. It just doesn't cut the Garou out of their tribe, it exiles them from the Garou Nation entirely. It's never been mentioned (AFAIK) that breed and auspice is somehow exempted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468842#post1468842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, ronin technically DO earn renown. Just at a VERY glacial pace.</div> </div> </div> </div>At first I thought, &quot;what is she thinking?&quot; so I decided to check the actual Rite of the Lone Wolf. And you're right. Both the 1e and 2e versions state that Ronin may continue to earn Renown, albeit at slower rank. 2e even says they may continue to rise in Rank! And while 1e does not state that explicitly, there is a vague statement that Ronin may continue to &quot;given the powers of Rank&quot; which can be interpreted in several ways.<br /> <br /> I totally missed that. However, in my defense, much of what is written about Ronin outside that Rite contradicts it. Even the 2e Players Guide, whose Rite of the Stolen Wolf stays Ronin could earn Renown and even Rank, has a later section that says since septs won't hear the stories of Ronin or perform the Rite of Accomplishment for them, that effectively it is impossible to earn Renown. Both Revised (in the Players Guide to Garou) and W20 explicitly state Ronin can't earn Renown, they can't earn Rank, and have no Rank within the Garou Nation. And if they should ever find a tribe that accepts them back, must start at Rank one (because they're considered to be a &quot;new&quot; person). <br /> <br /> I think one issue is that Revised and W20 (to my knowledge, I only have the W20 corebook) don't include the Rite of the Lone Wolf so it's never been updated. Plus I think in general, there's always been a lot of flaws and gaps in the books as important information about X seems to be forgotten (or perhaps purposefully ignored) the next time that subject is talked about, especially in new editions. Instead, writers seem to know the general idea about X and write a bunch of stuff based on it that sounds good, but which contradicts earlier material elsewhere. If Revised ever bothered to update the Rite of the Lone Wolf, it seems to me they would have had to make changes to reflect the stance it takes.<br /> <br /> It seems that later editions take a much harsher stance on Ronin than earlier ones. It's possible that the early editions just wanted Ronin to be equivalent of a &quot;Caitiff&quot; option and thus easier for a PC to be one in active play. Revised and W20 make it much harder for a PC Ronin to play with other PCs who are from tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1468360-spirits-gift-teaching-and-ronin?p=1468842#post1468842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if the ronin is one who rejected garou nation, they would not have even the breed or auspice ties. Depending on whether the ronin refuses 'magic' in general, they might try to avoid gifts or seek them out the 'human' way (ie. pagan summoning and such.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like Lost Cubs who reject the Garou. In these cases while such Garou would be considered &quot;Ronin&quot; socially and legally by the Garou since they remain outcasts, in most cases they would not have had the Rite of the Lone Wolf performed on them. And I think that matters because it's the rite that detaches the Garou from the Nation, and spirits have to respect that. At least in my interpretation, that Garou isn't &quot;marked&quot; so more things are possible. So in this case, I agree certain spirits may be more open to teaching Gifts to those Garou - provided they can figure things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T15:05:04-08:00","id":1468874,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if a ronin could &quot;create&quot; gift. Regardless any book rule, do you think it would be possible to invent a new power through meditation, by drawing on a spiritual source of energy or anything? In the case of a ronin, we could imagine that he seeks to develop his strength by himself, relying less on the assistance of the spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 11-25-2021, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:24:06-08:00","id":1468899,"title":"","content":"I asked before and will ask once more: where does the wording and circumstances of the Pact can be found and read?<br /> <br /> This is relevant, because while I understand the focus of the thread is to figure out spirits more likely to deal with Ronin and teach gifts, I'm strongly under the impression that you put yourself in a tight situation by making a too strict read of the spirits, how they behave and to what are they bound.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, most or all the Werewolf lore have one problem in this regard: an unreliable narrator. Even when the narrator is an OoC Third Person they can be unreliable, as the rules on spirit interaction are purposefully written from the PoV of the Garou Nation. AFAIK there are indications that the reality is somewhat different from the perspective of the spirits themselves. And although it wouldn't be enough to make a Ronin's life as easy as a Tribe Member's, it guards the crux of the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}